{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויעלו עולות", :translit "va'ya'alu olot", :gloss "and they offered burnt offerings"} {:he "בכורות", :translit "b'khorot", :gloss "firstborn (ones)"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויעלו עולות", :b "בכורות"}], :frame {:text "Before the Tabernacle was erected, the firstborn (b'khorot) Israelites served as priests, as stated at Exodus 24:5 where the designated young men of Israel's children offer burnt offerings. The shift of sacrificial service from firstborn to Levites follows the aftermath of the Golden Calf, described at Numbers 3:12–13 and Numbers 8:16–18, where the Levites are taken in place of the firstborn.", :sources ["Exodus 24:5" "Numbers 3:12–13" "Numbers 8:16–18"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויעלו עולות", :a-value 634, :b "בכורות", :b-value 634, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:20:29.422815938Z", :model "glm-5.2"}